choice BUDDY_PANEL
    prompt "Buddy display panel"
    default BUDDY_PANEL_ST77916_360
    help
        Selects the physical display the buddy firmware drives. The UI keeps
        its 360x360 logical canvas on both options; a smaller panel receives a
        downsampled copy of that canvas, so layout code stays panel-agnostic.

    config BUDDY_PANEL_ST77916_360
        bool "EchoEar-2ST 360x360 round (ST77916 over QSPI)"
        help
            The original companion screen. QSPI on SPI2_HOST, GPIO 3/4/5/6/7
            plus clock 8, reset 9, backlight 41.

    config BUDDY_PANEL_NV3023_240
        bool "Xingzhi-class 240x240 (NV3023 over SPI)"
        help
            The single-key 0.85-inch module (NV3023A, 240x240 visible window at
            GRAM row 80). SPI on SPI3_HOST, GPIO 9/10/8/14/18 and backlight 13.
            That wiring collides with the EchoEar audio pins, so this option
            also moves the speaker to the module's own I2S pins (DOUT 7 /
            BCLK 15 / WS 16, no MCLK) and skips touch, because GPIO 11/12 are
            this board's 4G modem UART rather than an I2C touch panel.
endchoice

config BUDDY_DISPLAY_SPI_CLOCK_MHZ
    int "Display SPI clock (MHz)"
    range 10 80
    default 20 if BUDDY_PANEL_ST77916_360
    default 40 if BUDDY_PANEL_NV3023_240
    help
        QSPI on the round panel is qualified at 20 MHz; the NV3023 module runs
        at 40 MHz on its short flex. Raising this is the first knob if a build
        shows tearing but is otherwise correct.
